avoid making mistakes altogether? That's an understandable response, but it turns out that demanding no errors might be the biggest mistake of all. This week on Hidden Brain. To air is human. When people work on things mistakes are inevitable. This is true in our personal lives, in our workplaces, and at the level of public policy. Not all mistakes are created equal though. Some failures are trivial, while others can be disastrous. At Harvard Business School, Amy Edminson studies how failures come about and what we can do about them. She has surprising insights into how organizations and people should think

