14
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:45.000
I saw that the p-value indicated that my data was statistically significant. So I was very excited. And then I looked more closely, leaning into the screen, and I realized that the sign was in the wrong direction. In other words, instead of seeing a relationship between good teamwork and low error rates. The statistical significance was saying there was a relationship between good teamwork and high error rates. How could that possibly be, Amy? Well, that was my question. And I set there. I think I froze. I was upset and I was scared. And so I set there looking at it. And my first reaction was, I must have made a mistake.

15
00:08:45.000 --> 00:09:10.000
I must have put the data in incorrectly. So I walked very carefully through everything I'd done. I redid it. And nope, maybe my hypothesis had been a mistake, but I had not made a kind of data entry mistake. And so there it was, staring at it again, and again puzzled. It just can't be true.

