error. So you hired a research assistant to actually go to the hospital and observe firsthand how teams at the hospital were functioning, testing this hypothesis that better teams in fact were more willing to report the mistakes, and that's why they were showing up as having committed greater numbers of mistakes. What did the research assistant find? Well, first of all, I think it's important to point out that I did not tell him what the survey data said, nor what the error data said.

